Frontier CLI - Command Line Interface for UserTalk Script Execution
Version 1.0.0 (Dec 17 2025)

Usage: ./frontier-cli [OPTIONS] [SCRIPT_FILE]

Execution Modes:
  Script Execution:
    ./frontier-cli script.usertalk                    # Execute UserTalk script file
    ./frontier-cli -e "3 + 4"                         # Execute inline script

  (Database and server modes will return an error until Phase 3 work completes.)

Options:
  -e, --execute SCRIPT     Execute inline UserTalk script
  -d, --database FILE      (disabled)
  -q, --query QUERY        (disabled)
  -m, --migrate            (disabled)
  --server                 (disabled)
  --websocket              (disabled)
  -p, --port PORT          (disabled)
  --system-root PATH       Load system root database before executing scripts
  -v, --verbose            Verbose output
  --debug                  Debug mode
  -h, --help               Show this help message
  --version                Show version information

Examples:
  # Execute a UserTalk script
  ./frontier-cli myscript.usertalk

  # Execute inline script
  ./frontier-cli -e "local(x = 5); x * 2"

  # Execute a script file
  ./frontier-cli myscript.usertalk

